--TEST--
`Core\Session::openWithIdentifier` takes an identifier the program read itself, and the first use of any other member reads it from the cookie, so every shape reaches the same store question -- `rule:core-api/session-roster`, `rule:core-classes/a-session-opens-on-its-first-use` and `rule:http-server/a-session-store-answers-five-operations`
--GET--
under=a-request
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The case answers a request, because every call shape below reaches the store
// question only through the one the open asks first
// (`rule:security/request-state-throws-in-an-isolate`).
//
// `rule:core-api/session-roster`'s signature is `openWithIdentifier(tainted string $id)`,
// the one explicit open, and every other member opens on its first use under
// the identifier the `[session] cookie` presented.
//
// What each call *does* is out of reach without a store, so the tree below
// chooses the shared tier and gives it no address. What is asserted is that all
// three reach the same place: the configured-store question, which is the first
// thing the open asks whatever it was handed. An open that fails leaves no
// session behind, so each call below opens again.
array<string> $shapes = [
    // The whole width of an identifier this store issues: 22 base64url
    // characters, which is what `mint` renders 128 drawn bits to.
    "PmA5tKz1QvR3sYbNqLwXe2",
    // And one it plainly did not — absence and a forgery are the same answer
    // under `rule:http-server/a-session-store-answers-five-operations`, so neither can be told from the other by which error arrives.
    "not-an-identifier",
];
uint $presented = 0;
foreach ($shapes as string $shape) {
    try {
        Core\Session::openWithIdentifier($shape);
    } catch (RuntimeError $unconfigured) {
        if (Core\Str::contains($unconfigured->message, "[cache.shared] url")) {
            $presented = $presented + 1;
        }
    }
}
echo "a presented identifier reached the store question ", $presented, " of 2\n";

// The first use, which is the ordinary case: the identifier is read from the
// `[session] cookie` field of the request rather than written at the call site.
uint $omitted = 0;
try {
    Core\Session::get("cart");
} catch (RuntimeError $unconfigured) {
    if (Core\Str::contains($unconfigured->message, "[cache.shared] url")) {
        $omitted = $omitted + 1;
    }
}
echo "a first use reached the same question ", $omitted, " of 1\n";
--FILE nvs.toml--
[session]
backend = "shared"
--EXPECT--
a presented identifier reached the store question 2 of 2
a first use reached the same question 1 of 1
